1
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:41,017
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,017 --> 00:02:45,017
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,017 --> 00:02:52,017
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,017 --> 00:02:58,017
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:58,017 --> 00:03:09,017
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,017 --> 00:03:13,017
I will be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:16,017 --> 00:03:24,017
During their journey to the New World, Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island, which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

8
00:03:24,017 --> 00:03:32,017
The Fishman Pirates, led by Horty Jones and assisted by Vander Decken, plot to overthrow King Neptune.

9
00:03:32,017 --> 00:03:40,017
It's not long before the Straw Hats get pulled into the conflict, which results in Horty detaining Zorro, Usopp, and Brook.

10
00:03:40,017 --> 00:03:44,017
Get out of my way, Team Bay. I won't let you keep me here anymore.

11
00:03:44,017 --> 00:03:47,017
Let me handle it. You stay put.

12
00:03:49,017 --> 00:03:54,017
Shut up! Sanji said all that cool stuff and you still want to fight?!

13
00:03:54,017 --> 00:03:58,017
If that is what it takes to make you listen to me, yes!

14
00:03:58,017 --> 00:04:00,017
What did you say?!

15
00:04:00,017 --> 00:04:01,017
Are you ready?

16
00:04:01,017 --> 00:04:02,017
Well, I was going to break my heart into lament…

17
00:04:02,017 --> 00:04:05,017
Can't Felix dig that out, Harley, David, jump up and you're wrong.

18
00:04:05,017 --> 00:04:07,017
Mā had got a good look for us but…

19
00:04:07,017 --> 00:04:08,017
Don't you.

20
00:04:08,017 --> 00:04:09,017
Don't you spill me?

21
00:04:09,017 --> 00:04:30,017
We also just popped up…

22
00:04:30,017 --> 00:04:32,017
are still alive.

23
00:04:35,017 --> 00:04:37,017
What a shot.

24
00:04:37,017 --> 00:04:44,017
The battle is on at Conchcord Plaza.

25
00:05:07,017 --> 00:05:17,017
Captain Horty sure is something else.

26
00:05:17,017 --> 00:05:20,017
One second he's writhing in agony he from an overdose,

27
00:05:20,017 --> 00:05:23,017
then he levels the whole town with a flick of his wrist.

28
00:05:37,017 --> 00:05:48,017
No. Neptune's army is done for. Every last one.

29
00:05:48,017 --> 00:05:52,017
They didn't stand a chance. Horty's too strong.

30
00:05:52,017 --> 00:05:55,017
We're all done for.

31
00:05:55,017 --> 00:05:59,017
Minister of the Right! Minister of the Left!

32
00:05:59,017 --> 00:06:02,017
King Neptune!

33
00:06:02,017 --> 00:06:05,017
Do something!

34
00:06:07,017 --> 00:06:10,017
We've wasted enough time onto the plaza.

35
00:06:13,017 --> 00:06:16,017
No! They're taking him away!

36
00:06:28,017 --> 00:06:31,017
We couldn't do anything.

37
00:06:37,017 --> 00:06:39,017
We were so close.

38
00:06:39,017 --> 00:06:40,017
You're going to be okay.

39
00:06:40,017 --> 00:06:42,017
After so long.

40
00:06:42,017 --> 00:06:45,017
Please stay with us.

41
00:06:45,017 --> 00:06:48,017
We were finally supposed to see results.

42
00:06:48,017 --> 00:06:52,017
This was going to be our year at the World Summit.

43
00:06:52,017 --> 00:06:54,017
Queen Otohime.

44
00:06:54,017 --> 00:06:57,017
But then they had to come and ruin everything.

45
00:06:57,017 --> 00:06:59,017
Someone help us!

46
00:06:59,017 --> 00:07:01,017
Save the king!

47
00:07:01,017 --> 00:07:04,017
If we don't stop them soon, he will be executed.

48
00:07:04,017 --> 00:07:07,017
Surely, someone can fight.

49
00:07:07,017 --> 00:07:08,017
What kind of fight?

50
00:07:22,017 --> 00:07:23,017
Look, Ma!

51
00:07:23,017 --> 00:07:39,017
This is the end of our whole country, isn't it?

52
00:07:39,017 --> 00:07:41,017
This is the end of our country, isn't it?

53
00:07:41,017 --> 00:07:42,017
This is the end of our country, isn't it?

54
00:07:42,017 --> 00:07:44,017
This is the end of our country.

55
00:07:44,017 --> 00:07:50,017
It's the end of our country who can't help you!

56
00:07:50,017 --> 00:08:04,957
Come on, Captain. Quit blubbering.

57
00:08:05,197 --> 00:08:08,377
Yeah, things will start looking up soon. Just get back in the game.

58
00:08:08,837 --> 00:08:12,457
Like I would ever take advice from a couple of losers like you.

59
00:08:12,617 --> 00:08:15,837
You guys have no idea what it's like having your heart broken.

60
00:08:15,837 --> 00:08:20,417
These feelings are real. I've wanted her since I first saw her.

61
00:08:20,657 --> 00:08:26,917
Sure, she was just a kid, but I knew if I married her, I could fulfill my ancestor's dream.

62
00:08:27,297 --> 00:08:29,337
But what happened instead?

63
00:08:41,197 --> 00:08:43,077
You're just not my type!

64
00:08:45,837 --> 00:08:48,757
Not my type, she said.

65
00:08:49,057 --> 00:08:52,557
When the words came to my ears, I felt my love grow.

66
00:08:53,257 --> 00:08:56,157
A flawless haiku by Vandertek in the night, I suspect.

67
00:08:57,297 --> 00:08:58,557
My soul.

68
00:08:59,137 --> 00:09:00,357
It's aching!

69
00:09:03,937 --> 00:09:08,537
After she rejected me, I felt like it was time for a change, so I cut my hair!

70
00:09:08,537 --> 00:09:10,897
I just attacked!

71
00:09:10,957 --> 00:09:13,857
I thought I'd kill her instead, but I can't even get that right!

72
00:09:14,097 --> 00:09:17,157
I know she's alive because I can still throw things at her!

73
00:09:17,297 --> 00:09:19,217
This is not Straw Hat's fault!

74
00:09:19,217 --> 00:09:19,837
Blah!

75
00:09:19,837 --> 00:09:20,757
Ha ha ha!

76
00:09:26,757 --> 00:09:28,617
Wait. That's it!

77
00:09:28,617 --> 00:09:34,977
What's so funny?

78
00:09:35,257 --> 00:09:35,997
My idea!

79
00:09:36,937 --> 00:09:42,017
If I can't end her existence, then I'll just have to end everyone else's!

80
00:09:43,297 --> 00:09:44,997
It's gonna be great!

81
00:09:44,997 --> 00:09:46,237
You'll see!

82
00:09:46,917 --> 00:09:47,917
Ha ha ha ha!

83
00:09:48,997 --> 00:09:51,097
Ha ha ha ha!

84
00:10:10,297 --> 00:10:10,617
Hmm?

85
00:10:10,617 --> 00:10:27,597
Release our king right now, Horty!

86
00:10:27,597 --> 00:10:28,777
Last warning!

87
00:10:40,617 --> 00:10:54,617
I mean it! We will fire!

88
00:10:54,617 --> 00:10:57,617
Run, soldiers! Don't throw your lives away!

89
00:10:57,617 --> 00:10:59,617
It's not that easy here!

90
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:01,617
Seabear!

91
00:11:10,617 --> 00:11:22,617
No!

92
00:11:22,617 --> 00:11:25,617
Take this, you bastard!

93
00:11:40,617 --> 00:11:56,617
Yeah, yeah, yeah! About time you got here! I was getting sick of waiting!

94
00:11:56,617 --> 00:11:58,617
We finally made it, Yozo!

95
00:11:58,617 --> 00:12:00,617
Be careful! He will cut you!

96
00:12:00,617 --> 00:12:05,617
I have arrived! At last!

97
00:12:05,617 --> 00:12:09,617
And now there is nowhere left for you to rot again.

98
00:12:10,617 --> 00:12:33,617
We can't get in! They locked the entrance to the plaza behind them!

99
00:12:33,617 --> 00:12:35,617
King Neptune!

100
00:12:35,617 --> 00:12:38,617
Let's scale the wall! Maybe we can see inside!

101
00:12:38,617 --> 00:12:45,617
This way! This way! This way! Hurry!

102
00:12:45,617 --> 00:12:48,617
Yes! Hurry!

103
00:12:48,617 --> 00:12:50,617
It's 5pm solid r possibilities!

104
00:12:50,617 --> 00:12:51,617
No!

105
00:12:51,617 --> 00:12:52,617
Let's go!

106
00:12:52,617 --> 00:12:53,617
Yeah!

107
00:12:53,617 --> 00:12:55,617
Seoul, look!

108
00:12:55,617 --> 00:13:00,617
Hmm...

109
00:13:00,617 --> 00:13:02,617
You can see!

110
00:13:02,617 --> 00:13:12,617
Uh...

111
00:13:12,617 --> 00:13:42,597
Oh, my God!

112
00:13:42,617 --> 00:13:49,177
It's settled.

113
00:13:49,757 --> 00:13:52,257
That boy sure gave me a lot of trouble, though.

114
00:13:53,897 --> 00:13:55,877
We've wasted far too much time.

115
00:13:56,177 --> 00:13:57,977
We need to be on our way now, Princess.

116
00:13:58,557 --> 00:13:59,037
Okay.

117
00:14:00,817 --> 00:14:03,077
We're leaving Hachi in your care, Kami.

118
00:14:03,717 --> 00:14:04,717
Uh, right.

119
00:14:06,417 --> 00:14:08,037
Let us make haste, Megalo.

120
00:14:08,037 --> 00:14:08,717
Ah!

121
00:14:12,617 --> 00:14:42,597
Let us make haste.

122
00:14:42,617 --> 00:14:58,177
I thought you soldiers were supposed to protect this country.

123
00:15:05,177 --> 00:15:06,337
My men.

124
00:15:06,337 --> 00:15:13,857
Damn you, Hordy.

125
00:15:19,437 --> 00:15:20,817
Look alive, boys.

126
00:15:20,997 --> 00:15:22,337
That soldier's up to something.

127
00:15:22,397 --> 00:15:24,317
You think so?

128
00:15:24,317 --> 00:15:27,417
Looks like he's packing dynamite.

129
00:15:27,617 --> 00:15:30,737
He's going to blow everyone up with some kind of suicide attack.

130
00:15:30,797 --> 00:15:34,677
But if he does that, I'm going to turn into roasted squid.

131
00:15:36,357 --> 00:15:38,697
The three princes should get here soon.

132
00:15:39,397 --> 00:15:42,317
But I can take out at least one of you before they do.

133
00:15:42,317 --> 00:15:51,757
Water shot.

134
00:15:51,817 --> 00:16:04,317
Oh, crap.

135
00:16:04,317 --> 00:16:10,497
How far can it go?

136
00:16:10,497 --> 00:16:33,457
You hear that?

137
00:16:33,457 --> 00:16:35,417
That whistling sound.

138
00:16:35,417 --> 00:16:49,417
What is it?

139
00:16:49,417 --> 00:16:59,777
And what is it?

140
00:16:59,777 --> 00:17:10,097
Hey, am I crazy?

141
00:17:10,697 --> 00:17:13,617
I was under the impression the water shot wasn't that strong.

142
00:17:21,137 --> 00:17:26,057
I know it took a lot of energy steroid to get that tough, but still, that was incredible!

143
00:17:26,057 --> 00:17:31,457
We never anticipated it changing your hair color or increasing your muscle mass so greatly, though.

144
00:17:31,457 --> 00:17:32,937
How are you feeling, Captain?

145
00:17:34,057 --> 00:17:35,177
Couldn't be better.

146
00:17:56,057 --> 00:17:57,697
What happened here?

147
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:01,577
Why didn't the soldiers wait for us to have them?

148
00:18:15,057 --> 00:18:17,897
Fukuboshi, Ryoboshi, Manboshi!

149
00:18:17,897 --> 00:18:19,577
Don't underestimate them.

150
00:18:19,577 --> 00:18:23,177
Both their ranks and their sea monsters have been empowered by a drug.

151
00:18:23,177 --> 00:18:24,457
Now it makes sense.

152
00:18:24,457 --> 00:18:28,857
On an even playing field, Neptune's army would never lose a sortie-do!

153
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:30,377
It's time to mumble!

154
00:18:30,377 --> 00:18:31,177
Ready?

155
00:18:47,897 --> 00:18:56,457
Why don't you understand?

156
00:18:57,097 --> 00:18:58,297
You're all so pathetic!

157
00:18:58,857 --> 00:19:01,657
You new fishman pirates are just a bunch of cowards!

158
00:19:02,457 --> 00:19:07,337
The other islanders let go of their hurt feelings brought on by the humans' discrimination.

159
00:19:07,337 --> 00:19:12,617
And despite the fact that humans murdered their hero and their queen, they're willing to forgive them.

160
00:19:12,617 --> 00:19:19,177
Even after all of their suffering, they still sign their names, because they want to change the future!

161
00:19:20,057 --> 00:19:20,777
Your Highness.

162
00:19:21,337 --> 00:19:22,457
Prince Fukuboshi.

163
00:19:25,497 --> 00:19:28,057
What you do undermines their efforts!

164
00:19:28,057 --> 00:19:30,057
Can't you recognize their bravery?

165
00:19:31,417 --> 00:19:32,617
You're kidding me, right?

166
00:19:33,977 --> 00:19:36,057
Don't mistake their kindness for courage.

167
00:19:36,617 --> 00:19:39,737
It gives the humans another excuse to take advantage of us.

168
00:19:42,617 --> 00:19:47,177
We're of the ages!

169
00:19:48,377 --> 00:19:50,857
Seven princesses!

170
00:19:50,857 --> 00:19:52,857
Dragon Tower Gate!

171
00:19:58,537 --> 00:20:01,017
The princess beat the sea monsters!

172
00:20:01,017 --> 00:20:03,257
There's hope after all!

173
00:20:03,897 --> 00:20:08,377
You seek revenge not for justice, but because of your own personal hatred.

174
00:20:08,377 --> 00:20:12,617
I won't let you take the king's life, nor the island his citizens call home!

175
00:20:13,417 --> 00:20:15,817
You will never have the Ryugu Kingdom!

176
00:20:22,217 --> 00:20:23,417
We're safe!

177
00:20:23,417 --> 00:20:25,657
We should have known we could count on the princes!

178
00:20:25,657 --> 00:20:33,497
So you beat some sea monsters.

179
00:20:33,497 --> 00:20:35,657
Do you think that means you've claimed victory?

180
00:20:36,617 --> 00:20:41,737
We will never be defeated, because we've been granted a power that is absolute.

181
00:20:43,417 --> 00:20:48,057
And with that power, we will rule this country the way it was always meant to be.

182
00:20:48,057 --> 00:20:51,497
The future of this country is peace!

183
00:20:51,497 --> 00:20:54,857
Peace with the humans, and peace with the monsters like you!

184
00:20:54,857 --> 00:20:59,977
If we don't triumph here, we'll have failed, and it will be hundreds of years before we have another

185
00:20:59,977 --> 00:21:01,897
shot at friendship with the human world!

186
00:21:01,897 --> 00:21:03,737
Oh, is that a fact?

187
00:21:05,577 --> 00:21:09,977
Well, then the winners of this fight will rule this country.

188
00:21:09,977 --> 00:21:26,697
It's a good happening!

189
00:21:29,217 --> 00:21:29,977
Hmm.

190
00:21:29,977 --> 00:21:32,137
Oh...

191
00:21:35,497 --> 00:21:36,957
Whoa!

192
00:21:36,977 --> 00:21:37,417
Hey!

193
00:21:37,417 --> 00:21:44,617
They look... stronger!

194
00:21:51,157 --> 00:21:52,797
What? But how?

195
00:21:54,257 --> 00:21:55,717
Too slow.

196
00:22:07,417 --> 00:22:08,417
Huh?

197
00:22:08,417 --> 00:22:09,417
Huh?

198
00:22:09,417 --> 00:22:10,417
Ah!

199
00:22:10,417 --> 00:22:11,417
Ah!

200
00:22:11,417 --> 00:22:12,417
Ah!

201
00:22:17,417 --> 00:22:19,417
Roar!

202
00:22:19,417 --> 00:22:20,417
Roar!

203
00:22:29,417 --> 00:22:31,417
Time is running short, Megalo.

204
00:22:31,417 --> 00:22:32,417
Ja!

205
00:22:32,417 --> 00:22:34,417
Be safe, Father.

206
00:22:34,417 --> 00:22:36,417
We'll be there soon.

207
00:22:36,417 --> 00:22:38,417
He's going to be fine.

208
00:22:38,417 --> 00:22:40,417
I promise you, Princess.

209
00:22:51,417 --> 00:22:55,417
This drug of yours is fearsome indeed, Horty.

210
00:22:57,417 --> 00:23:00,417
Ja-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

211
00:23:00,417 --> 00:23:03,417
Ja-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

212
00:23:06,417 --> 00:23:12,417
Shirohoshi and Jinbei hurry to Concord Plaza to free King Neptune.

213
00:23:12,417 --> 00:23:15,417
But their rescue plan is cut short by a trap.

214
00:23:15,417 --> 00:23:21,417
With the royal family now captured, Horty reveals a shocking truth about the history of his revolution.

215
00:23:21,417 --> 00:23:26,417
While the island is seized with despair, Van Der Decken does something rash.

216
00:23:26,417 --> 00:23:29,417
On the next, One Piece, a surprising confession.

217
00:23:29,417 --> 00:23:32,417
The truth behind the assassination of Otohime.

218
00:23:32,417 --> 00:23:34,417
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

219
00:23:34,417 --> 00:23:36,417
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

220
00:23:36,417 --> 00:23:38,417
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

